{
	// zappy at full scale, in d minor. 30 bars, 65.15 s, five tempos.
	//
	// the plan. the ident's motif (a d e a | f#), stated, darkened, built,
	// broken and brought back larger. the key is d minor with its two
	// chords from below, b flat and c, which climb back to d: the chords
	// of a film's last reel. (zappy-big-phrygian is the same piece in the
	// other key, to choose between.)
	//
	//   1-4   plain, 92 a minute, a clock ticking the beats. the motif
	//         alone on the driven saw with low brass under it, and the ident's b flat
	//         floor under its last note (bar 2). then the motif again,
	//         and this time it lands on f, not f#: minor (bar 4), over a
	//         bare d. the tune has been told what key it is really in.
	//   5-8   build, 104. the bass starts to run in eighths, a kick on
	//         one and three. the minor motif with a tail (f e d); then
	//         the motif a fourth higher over b flat and c (d g a d | bb
	//         a g). chords: dm dm bb c.
	//   9-12  build, 116. the motif at double speed, one to a bar, each
	//         bar starting higher: from a, from c, from d, from e. the
	//         brass in a three-three-two push. chords: dm f bb a. the a
	//         chord is major (c#) and pulls hard; its last beat is a
	//         rest in everything but a snare roll.
	//   13-20 destruction, 132, everything ff. the motif's first three
	//         notes (a d e) hammered twice a bar in octaves, then its
	//         last two (a, f) as two long blows, the bass in sixteenths.
	//         the same hammering holds while the chords fall under it by
	//         thirds, dm dm bb bb gm gm (the tune moves down for gm: g c
	//         d | g e flat), then a, an a major arpeggio hammered, and
	//         bar 20 is one blow on the first beat and nothing after.
	//   21-22 break, 72. near silence: the clock, slower, and the ident
	//         alone, pp, in the major, a d e a | f#. nothing under it.
	//   23-30 return, 120. the motif at half speed in octaves, an octave
	//         lower than it has been, over b flat, c and then d major
	//         with every voice: bb c d d. then once more at speed over bb
	//         c, landing on d for two bars and one last blow. the lowest
	//         bass of the piece is here (b flat 0, c1, d1).
	//
	// drums: from bar 13 a kick on every beat with a clap on two and
	// four and a hat between; a crash on the first beat of bars 13, 17
	// and each second bar of the return; kick, tom and crash together
	// for the two last blows (bars 20 and 30).
	//
	// time: the clock of bars 1 to 4 is the beat of everything after it,
	// and the piece is that clock driven faster in steps, 92, 104, 116,
	// 132, until it breaks; the break is the clock alone again, slowed.
	//
	// loud and quiet: 1-4 mp and mf; 5-10 mf; 11-12 f; 13-20 ff; 21-22
	// pp; 23-30 ff. the return has more voices than the first statement
	// (octaves, five-note chords, two bass notes, drums) at the top mark.
